nterterrorism tool is bigotry. I'm saying there's a real, meaningful difference between "target specific organizations/individuals based on actual intelligence" (which is how legitimate counterterrorism works, however imperfectly) and "treat an entire 1.8-billion-person religious category as suspect because of a subset's actions" (which is what your colleague is facing, and which even government's own tools, when they tried it that way, produced nothing useful).
